[
    {
        "content": "<p>In a recent local build of Algolean, I ran into a proof widgets issue in which the error message explicitly suggested that I should report on Zulip. To quote the error message:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">✖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">267</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">790</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Building</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">proofwidgets</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">widgetJsAll</span>\n<span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProofWidgets</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reuse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pre</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">built</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">JS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">code</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Please</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">report</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">issue</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Zulip</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 587772662,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776693307
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><strong>Update</strong> : This issue is fixed by running <code>lake update proofwidgets</code> fixes the issue. This is strange because I did not face this issue before when running <code>lake build</code> on the same toolchain. The only difference was adding PhysLib as a dependency. </p>\n<p>Toolchain : v4.29.0</p>",
        "id": 587779773,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776694939
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113489\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/ProofWidgets.20failed.20to.20re-use.20pre-built.20JS.20code/with/584596331\">#new members &gt; ProofWidgets failed to re-use pre-built JS code</a></p>",
