    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/Shreyas4991/Algolean\">https://github.com/Shreyas4991/Algolean</a></p>",
        "id": 587808659,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776701852
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I tried to reproduce by doing  (on a fresh clone) </p>\n<p>1) <code>git checkout b88523bbcbf9d8a3fff26251d6b15f44239f09ca</code> (before the physlib bump)<br>\n2) <code>lake build</code><br>\n3) adding physlib as a dependency<br>\n4) <code>lake update Physlib</code><br>\n5) <code>lake build</code></p>\n<p>I couldn't reproduce, but something interesting is that on <code>lake update Physlib</code> we get a different mathlib due to URL mismatch</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mathlib</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">URL</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">changed</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deleting</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'~/</span><span class=\"n\">downstreams</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Algolean</span><span class=\"bp\">/.</span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">packages</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cloning</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">again</span>\n<span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mathlib</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cloning</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">github</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">com</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">leanprover</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">community</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">git</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>You can see that <a href=\"https://github.com/Shreyas4991/Algolean/commit/6416859fd903dcd05351c016d96e4e3285c3bc41\">in the lake manifest change too</a></p>",
        "id": 587809421,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Lynch",
        "timestamp": 1776702059
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>that is to be expected right? Physlib is on v4.29.1 since today morning</p>",
        "id": 587809684,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776702131
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That means there is a <code>lake exe cache</code> on mathlib happening, so it might be related...</p>",
        "id": 587809696,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Lynch",
        "timestamp": 1776702133
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am compiling with both cslib and Physlib on v4.29.0</p>",
        "id": 587809789,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776702158
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And updating proofwidgets somehow fixed this error.</p>",
        "id": 587809825,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776702168
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"466334\">Shreyas Srinivas</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/More.20ProofWidgets.20issues/near/587809684\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>that is to be expected right? Physlib is on v4.29.1 since today morning</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It would be nice for <code>lake</code> to realize that <code>https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4.git</code> and <code>https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4</code> are the same thing (the <code>.git</code> suffix is irrelevant)</p>",
        "id": 587809895,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Lynch",
        "timestamp": 1776702178
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(tbh I don't expect this to be related to the cache issue, but it surprised me)</p>",
